# Component BEM Styling

All component styles must use [BEM](https://getbem.com/) (Block Element Modifier) naming.

## Structure

```
block               → the component root        (.card)
block__element      → a part of the component   (.card__header)
block--modifier     → a variant of the block    (.card--compact)
block__element--modifier → a variant of an element (.fold__trigger--open)
```

## Rules

- The **block** name matches the component's CSS class on its root element and is always **lowercase** (e.g. `card`, `fold`)
- **Elements** are separated from the block with double underscore `__`
- **Modifiers** are separated from the block or element with double dash `--`
- Never use more than one level of element nesting — `block__element__sub` is **not** valid BEM; introduce a new element name instead
- Class names are **kebab-case** only — no camelCase, no PascalCase

## File Conventions

- Each component has its own `styles.css`; styles are never shared across components
- Group selectors inside the file by block → elements → modifiers, with a comment header for each group:

```css
/* ── Header ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
```

## Reference Implementations

- [src/components/Fold/styles.css](mdc:src/components/Fold/styles.css)
- [src/components/Card/styles.css](mdc:src/components/Card/styles.css)

## Examples

```css
/* ✅ correct */
.card { }
.card__header { }
.card__section { }
.card__label { }
.card--compact { }
.fold__trigger--open { }

/* ❌ incorrect */
.card__header__title { }   /* double nesting */
.cardHeader { }            /* camelCase */
.card_header { }           /* single underscore */
.card-header { }           /* ambiguous — looks like a modifier separator */
```
